      "Language": "ger",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "There is a causal relationship between smoking and the development of lung-cancer, coronary heart disease, peripheral occlusion disease and cerebral thromboembolic complications. Lobectomy, pneumonectomy or palliative measurements are necessary in the treatment of lung-cancer. Transluminal dilatation with a balloon catheter and vascular surgery may be effective in removing of isolated stenoses or artery occlusions."},
